WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.290
In 1990, 6.6 million people born
in India lived in other countries.

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:13.410
By 2024, the UN estimates 18.5 million
people born in India living abroad:

3
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.870
more than from any other country.

4
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.990
China and Mexico come next.

5
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.350
The largest group lives in the
United Arab Emirates: 3.25 million.

6
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.150
Then the USA and Saudi Arabia.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.730
How do they change places at both ends?

8
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.950
Only through the money they send home?

9
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.470
Only in the Gulf?

10
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.730
In this mission, you'll find
out who counts as the diaspora,

11
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.450
and why official totals
differ: 18.5 million,

12
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.290
or 37.3 million?

13
00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.370
Then you'll follow the
links home to Kerala,

14
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.670
in south-west India, and abroad
to Leicester, in England.

15
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.790
Your mission: explain how India's
diaspora changes places at both ends.
